  "description_short": "Waterfront dining at The Point with fresh seafood, ocean views, and relaxed Mossel Bay vibes.",
  "description_long": "Perched right at The Point on Mossel Bay's historic harbour, Kingfisher Restaurant delivers what every coastal town needs: honest seafood with a view. The setting is unbeatable – waves breaking just metres away, fishing boats bobbing in the bay, and that salty Garden Route breeze drifting through the covered deck. It's the kind of spot where locals bring visiting family and tourists stumble upon something special.\n\nThe menu leans heavily into what the ocean provides: linefish done simply, calamari that actually tastes like the sea, and proper fish and chips. There's plenty for non-seafood eaters too, with steaks, burgers, and pasta keeping everyone happy. Service can be leisurely when it's busy, but that's part of the charm – you're here for the location as much as the meal.\n\nWhether you're stopping for lunch after exploring the Cape St Blaize lighthouse or settling in for sundowners with the harbour as your backdrop, Kingfisher captures that easy-going Mossel Bay spirit. Book ahead for weekends and school holidays, especially if you want a table on the deck.",
